static const char*const npcDialoguePages54a[]={"Man... When you travel all around the world, you'll hear of\nsome crazy things.","Once, I heard that there are Cards which contain the power\nof monsters. If someone happens to get their hands on a\ncard, they'll be able to use that monster's power.","I'm guessing it's some sort of fad or scam, where they make\nyou collect all the cards or whatever. I mean, how can a\ncard really hold the power of a monster?!","Seriously...","Oh...!\nWelcome to Alberta,\nyoung adventurer!","Pardon me if I seem distracted. I'm milling about, trying to\nmake a plan. You see, I hear that there is a store in Geffen\nthat sells armor that is resistant to magic.","If I buy a lot of them in bulk, and then resell them here\nfor a higher price...","People say the legendary weapon Gungnir never misses its\ntarget. I wonder if it's possibly true...","People also say that babies are assembled by the storks\nbefore delivery, girls dig guys who act like jerks, and that\nSanta Claus exists! But only in Lutie.","I wonder...\nIf any of that\nis possibly\ntrue...","Some time ago,\na derelict ship\ndrifted into\nAlberta harbour.","Hoping to save any survivors, some of the townspeople\nventured into the ship. However, they all ran out terrified,\nsaying that corpses were walking around inside the ship.","The ship was also packed with dangerous marine organisms,\nand they couldn't get inside, even if they wanted to.","We couldn't do anything about that ominous looking ship, and\njust left it as it was. Nowadays, exploration teams try to\nenter that ship and wipe out its monsters.","So it might be a good experience for a young person like\nyourself to be a recruit. But, it's still not worth risking\nyour life if you're not strong enough.","Aren't level 4 weapons cool!\nI can't believe such powerful\nweapons exist!","Well, they're rarely seen in the open market, but boss\nmonsters will drop them by a low chance if you happen to be\nable to kill them.","You don't have to listen to a guy right next to my room.\nTwo years ago, he was in a mercenary training center and\nfell off from a tree\nwhile trying to gather a nut from it.","He keeps talking to himself loud and it gives me a\nheadache...\nGosh!","I usually come to this well to\ndraw water, but never when it's\nfoggy or rainy. For some reason\nwhenever the weather is a\ncertain way, I feel like...","...someone...or some thing is\nstruggling to crawl out from\nthe bottom of this well...\nIt really gives me the creeps.","Yo~\nYou're not from around here.\nHeh, another outsider.\nJust like me...","It's been five long years\nsince I've started doing\nbusiness here...","Af first, I thought, 'What\na great chance!' when the\ntrade between the Rune-Midgard\nKingdom and Amatsu started.","I wanted to do something great\nand make the most of this\nnew opportunity.","And so, I decided to go to\nAmatsu so I could learn to make\nAmatsu cuisine. Then, I could\nreturn to my hometown and make\nthis exotic food for everyone.","But, I fell in love with Amatsu\nand I ended up sticking around\nhere for the last five years.\nDuring all that time, I've\nbeen learning Amatsu cuisine,","and cooking these dishes for\nthe towners, and enjoying myself\nby talking to the locals,\ntransfixed in this very spot.","But recently, across the street,\nthe Sushi Master opened his shop.\n...\nNow, my only customers are flies.","I was hoping to fulfill my\ndream of becoming a renowned chef\nin Amatsu, but...\nI guess it's over...","Puhuhu~!\nDid you see Miss Amatsu near\nthe Harbor? Isn't she\npreeeetty?","I'm going to enter the Miss\nAmatsu Contest when I'm older.","I'm sure that I'm the prettiest\nin this town but...\nA lady can always use a little more makeup.","I'm worried about my husband.\nHe lost a lot of money in some distant town today.","I got so mad at him, he ran off in\nfear! I'm worried...what if he\nwent to the bar and starts drinking again? The man just\ndoesn't have any backbone. *Phew*","This place is special to me.\nIt's filled with memories of my wife.","It was under that big tree where\nI first told her I loved her. At\nthe time, I really didn't know that she also had feelings\nfor me.","After that day, we had many\nconversations here. Quiet\nand peaceful, this was our\nfavorite place to be together.","When I close my eyes here, I\ncan picture our good times,\nand it feels like it all happened yesterday.\n...","My wife passed away...\nSo now I only come here by\nmyself...But I feel like I'm with her whenever I'm here.","Do you have anyone that you\nthink about? If you have a\nspecial someone, don't hesitate\nor hold back. Be sure to treat\nthat person specially.","Human beings live such short\nlives. But we're able to laugh\nthroughout life and forget the\nsadness.\n...Always be happy.","There's an ancient,\ndreadful building in\nAyotaya that no one\nhere dares approach...","In the past, a few curious people went inside, despite the\nhorror stories, and never returned. What on earth could be\ngoing on inside of that place?","However, if you want to prove your courage to others,\nconfronting the danger inside might be a worthy challenge\nfor an adventurer...\nI think.","Ummm.\nHmmmmm...\nUmmmmm...?","You must be\nan outsider.\nYes. Yes, indeed.","Did you just ask\nwhere am I going?\nWhy, to the Fishing Spot\njust ahead. That's what\nwe old men do: fish.","Hmmm...\nWould you like to hear\nsomething interesting? I've heard that someone found a ring\ninside\na fish he caught in the\nFishing Spot.","Supposedly, there are lots of stories about people finding\nvaluables inside of the fish they've been catching there.","If you're lucky enough,\nyou might even become\na millionaire.\nHeh heh heh~","...!?\nAh, I came into the fish market! *Sigh* It seems I went the\nwrong way. The Fishing Spot is on the opposite side of this\nvillage.","Since I'm here, it wouldn't be\na bad idea to look around. All of the seafood in this market\nis fresh and tasty. You'll regret it if you don't try some\nof this seafood\nat least once.","Phew, isn't it\nsoooo hot today?","You must be\nfrom Rune-Midgard, huh?\nI've seen a lot of tourists\ncoming from there recently.","You'd better be really careful if you travel outside of the\nvillage. Whatever you do, don't go into\nthe ruins of an old shrine\nin the forest.","That place is far too\ndangerous to visit. Still, I hear that if you had some kind\nof amulet, you could go there with\na little less worry...","Well, anyway, it's still a really good idea to stay away\nfrom that place. I hope you enjoy visiting Ayotaya, and that\nyou keep safe~","In Ayotaya, we have our own traditional martial arts. We,\nthe young men of the village, practice our traditional\nmartial arts in order to become strong.","Why don't you learn our martial arts? I guarantee that it\nwill help you greatly in your travels.","Gambling...? The games\nprovided here in the Comodo\nCasino are a higher form of\nentertainment than gambling.\nDo you know what I mean?","Granted, I did lose\nall of my zeny playing\nin this Casino, but I have\nno regrets. I'll simply earn\nmore money, then blow it all\nagain. Or I just might win big!","Bwahahahaahah~!\nYes, I can only lose so\nmany times until I hit the\njackpot! You see, you see?\nI'm playing the freakin' odds.","Damn it! Where did that\nguy go? He promised me that\nhe'd easily double my money!\nWait. Oh, wait. Oh... Oh no...","Don't tell me that I just got\nconned out of my money!\nOh no! Still, I better report\nthis to the proper authorities,\nno matter how ashamed I feel...","Heh heh heh...\nWhaaaat a gullible\nguy. I took his money\nso easily! I mean, I didn't\neven come up with that great\nof a lie, and he gave it to me!","All I need is for this\nlittle steel bead to fall\ninto the right hole. Then,\nI'll win the jackpot. Alright.\nHere goes. One last time...","No! No, I was so close!\nAlright, next time I should\nbe even closer, right? Yeah.\nOkay, this time will be the\nlast time. Not again! Alright,\nj-just one more t-time...","Oh, I'm sorry, sir,\nbut it looks like you\nlost again. Maybe you\nshould quit for now...\nYou've been having quite\na run of really bad luck...","N-no...\nI lost again?!\nBut I can't quit like\nthis! I'm gonna keep\ngoing, and I'm gonna\nleave this place a winner!","The more I think about it,\nit seems easier to become\nrich by working, saving, and\nmaking wise investments than\nto, you know... Rely on some\nkind of huge jackpot prize.","Gambling seems fun, but\nit seems smarter to make\nmoney in other ways. Sure,\nworking hard is no fun, but\nthere are ways to use your money to make more of it, right?","There's also the matter of\nbeing smart and responsible\nabout your money--I mean, you're more likely to blow all\nyour cash\nif you win it, right? Yeah, you\ngotta be wise about it all...","People call me the\nSea Lady because I'm\nalways here working,\ngathering clams and other\nsea creatures to sell. It's\na pretty good living, actually.","It's nice to be able to work\noutdoors, but someday, I want\nto save enough money and move\nto the city. I'm still young, you know, and I've got dreams\nthat I want to fulfill~","Ahhh, it's nice being\na fisherman. You just\nrelax and let the fish\ncome to you. Well, it takes\nsome skill to catch as much\nfish as I do with no effort~","I like the leisure involved\nin my job, but if it's not one\nthing, it's another. Yeah, that\ndaughter of mine over there\nwon't stop harping about\nmoving to the biiig city.","Why does she want to leave\nme so badly?! But if I don't\nlet her go, she'll run away.\nWhat am I going to do with\nthat girl? Well, I can't really\nstop her from dreaming...","I love playing in\nthe sand-- it's so soft\nand clean and pretty!\nBut when I grow up,\nI wanna go to Alberta\nand see everything I can!","Hello, this is one of the\nlighthouses that make up\nParos Lighthouse. However,\nright now it's undergoing\nrenovation, so it's not\nopen to the public.","Wow...\nAn adventurer from\nRune-Midgarts, eh?\nWhat brings you here?","Einbech doesn't offer much\nin terms of sight-seeing, but\nhave you come to see the mine?\nRight now, it's swarming with\nmonsters and we can't dig any\nores because it's so dangerous.","Now, if some adventurers were\ngenerous enough to hunt down\nthose evil creatures, we'd be able to mine again and they\ncould earn some extra zeny. It's like killing two birds with\none stone. Hahaha!","Oh wait... I'm sorry.\nI don't know what's wrong\nwith me, asking complete\nstrangers to do favors for\nme. It's completely rude!\nI mean, who would do that?","But... I'm beyond caring\nabout my pride. For the sake\nof all that is good and holy, I'm begging you, please kill\nthose foul and evil creatures. Please~!","Recently, there were a few\ncave-ins where many miners\nwere injured. It was discussed\nin the Town Council and in my\nopinion, I think the miners dug\ntoo deep and disturbed... it.","Yes, they awoke Ungoliant,\nthe master of the caves that\nhas existed since ancient time.\nI don't know how many more will\nbe victimized by Ungoliant in the\nfuture. There's no telling...","Adventurer, be careful\nif you travel inside the\nmines, lest your footsteps\ndisturb Ungoliant's slumber.","Those Einbroch bastards!\nLiving off the resources we\ndig up while we keep working\nfor them like suckers! Damn!","Everyday, we risk our\nfreakin' lives just so we\ncan make a living! Why don't\nthe elders do something about\nthis, like raise our ore prices?","The work schedule's\nunreasonable, Cavitar's\nwife was attacked by a mine\ncreature, the hospital's too\nfar away and we don't have\nany food to eat! Why...?!","I've lived here a long time\nand, believe it or not, things\nweren't as tough in the past\nas they are right now.","For lots of different reasons,\nthe work is more dangerous\nand we're running real low on\nmanpower. And the factories in\nEinbroch make so much smog,\nwe can't even see sunlight here.","The sad reality of mining\nlife right now is that we\nwake up, go to work, and at\nthe end of the day, some of us\nare injured while a few others never come to work the next\nday.","And as Einbech and Einbroch\nhave grown, I hear more and\nmore rumors that unfamiliar\nmonsters are beginning to\nswarm outside of town. This\nis really Einbech's worst time...","This train station\nis strictly for trains\nrunning from Einbech\nto Einbroch. Please speak\nto the staff in the 11 'o clock direction if you'd like to\nboard.","Ah...!\nThis is killing me!\nI don't have the money\nto move, but I don't wanna\nlive in this town anymore!","People everywhere else\nlive so much better than we\ndo, especially those snobs in\nEinbroch! Einbech must be the\nworst town Schwaltzvalt Republic. No, it's the worst in the\nworld!","I don't get it!\nEinbroch gets bigger\nand fancier and our\ntown gets dirtier and\nnastier. What the hell?!","Not only do the people\nhere look more ragged, we're\nmore tired and older looking\neven! It's dirty, it's crowded,\neverything in this city is total crap! What, you want a\nlist?!","The food, literally, is\ngarbage! The jobs here have\nto be violations of human rights. There's barely any women\nhere and the ones we do have are all stank anyway! Are you\nconvinced yet?!","Why is everything\nthat's good over in\nEinbroch?! I hate this!\n*Grumble*","It's hard being a woman\nin this town. By being born\nhere, it's like fate just decided to be especially cruel to\nme.","My skin and hands are\nrough from all the work\nI have to do. But worst of\nall... I... I... I've developed\nbigger muscles than most\nguys! Waaaaaah~!","I wish I could find\na nice guy from Einbroch\nand get married so I can\nget away from this town.\nBut it doesn't look like\nthat will happen...","And I'd never marry\nanyone from Einbech!\nI'd rather die cold and\nalone than cold and married\nto some Einbech hooligan.","Look at these\nmuscles. What do\nyou think? Am I pretty?\n*Sniff* I gave up trying\nto be feminine years ago.\nI have to work so hard...","Yo-heave-ho!\nYo-heave-ho~!","What am I doing here?\nHeck, I'm scared to death\nof entering the mine! But\nI can make a living here at\nthe entrance by gathering\nscrap metal! Smart, huh?","Sometimes, I get lucky\nand score an entire ore!\nSure, I'm a coward, but\nat least I'm alive. Well,\nfor the time being.","Now you know what\nI'm doing here. So why\ndon't you leave me to\nmy work? Heave-ho!\nOres, come to me!","\n Mine Dungeon Entrance\n","\n Train Station\n","\n Freight Train Station\n","\n Tool Shop\n","\n Tavern\n","Welcome to 'Einbech'.","East - Tavern, Tool Shop\nNorth - Train Station, Mine Dungeon","Northwest - Train Station\nSouth - Tavern\nNorth - Tool Shop, Mine Dungeon","Most Einbech men are\ncrude and primitive male\nchauvinists! They disgust me!","I mean, there's nothing\ngood about them! They're\nwild, violent, simple minded\nand ignorant. They settle all\ntheir arguments with brawn\nand they're so... close minded!","How can they not know\nthat women want gentle,\nsensitive men with whom\nthey can share their feelings\nand drink chamoille tea over\nfreshly knit doilies?","...*Hiccup*...\n*Hiccup*...\n*Yawn*.....\n.................\n..*Hiccup*.....\n*Hiccup*..","*Cough cough!*\nLaaaand sakes!","An old woman like me\ncan't breathe this air! How\ndo people even live in all this\nsmog? Sure, the air in Einbech\nisn't pristine, but the air here in Einbroch is much worse!\n*Cough~!*","I hate coming here\nsometimes! The air is\ntotally polluted and this\ncity is full of stuck up\npricks! But they sell stuff\nhere I can't buy back home...","All the factories\nhere in Einbroch are\ncausing a serious air\npollution problem.","I'm an Airship engineer and\neveryday, all day long, I deal\nwith oil stains and all sorts\nof pollutants. I'm surprised\nI haven't gotten sick yet...","Still, I try to be careful\nwhen I can. Whenever I go\nout into the city's red fog,\nI always wear my Flu Mask.\nIf you'll be here for a while,\nyou should carry one with you.","Excuse me...\nBut I'm lost!\nI can't find my\nmom or dad!","A-am I at the Airport?!\nMy parents are supposed\nto come get me, but I still\nhaven't found them! We just\nmoved here, so I don't know\nwhere anything is!","W-wait!\nWhere are you\ngoing?! Don't leave\nme, I'm all alone...!","I've lived here for\na long time and I see\nthat this huge city is still\ngrowing bigger everyday.","How did Einbroch get so\nhuge so quickly? I still can't\nbelieve there's been this much\ndevelopment. Well, I suppose\nit's not my concern. Nothing\nI do will make a difference...","Even though such\nrapid industrialization\ncan't be good for the\nenvironment or the people,\nI'll just sit back, watch what\nhappens and just enjoy life...","*Cough cough*\nJiminy! The air here\nis so thick and grimy!\nAnd it's worse for us old\npeople with breathing\nproblems! *Haaack!*","I don't care if they keep\nbuilding more and more\nfactories and homes in this\ntown. Still, I'd like to spend\nthe rest of my life somewhere\nquiet and with clean air...","Then again, Einbroch is my\nhometown and I can't just up\nand leave. I suppose it's my\nfate to suffer from this foul air until the day I die.\n*Sigh...*","Lately, there's been\ntalk about this empty\nbuilding downtown that's\nbeen converted into some\nsort of mysterious facility.","It all seems pretty\nshady, but I guess it's\nnot really my job to know\nabout that. I mean, if it\ndoesn't affect me, why\nshould I be concerned?","Surprisingly, we have\na Train Station that everyone\nhas been calling a victory for\nscience. I mean, shouldn't we\nbe more amazed by the Airship?","Now, if you want to know\nwhere the train actually goes,\nI wouldn't be able to tell you.\nAfter all, I never rode it. But\nstill, I guess having our own\nTrain Station is a good thing.","...And that's why\nI travel around the\nglobe. My bosses have\na keen eye for the most\nexotic goods, so I acquire\nthem and make deliveries.","There even was a time\nwhen they had me collect\nJellopy, though that stuff is\npretty common nowadays.\nNow that I think about it, why\ndid they need so much stuff?","Now, I hear that the\nmonsters around here\ncarry around some ore\nthat dazzles with a sublimely\nbeautiful light. Neat, huh?","These ores are a great\nmaterial to use in making\nflower vases. My friend, who\nhappens to be a dollmaker,\ntold me that. He makes these dolls using all sorts of\nmaterials.","He fashions them out of\nWell-Tanned Leather, stuffs\nthem with Bird Feathers, and\nuses Cyfar or Zargon to make\nthe eyes. He even uses a Jellopy at the bottom to balance\nthe doll.","I guess that goes to show\nthat things that seem useless\nmight actually be handy in some\nway. So don't worry about having too much stuff. Sooner or\nlater, it might be useful to someone.","If you just pay me money,\nI'll be your slave! There's\nnothing I won't do! Anything\nis fair game. Hell, I'll get buck naked if you pay me\nenough.","If you pay me what I'm\nworth, I'll work hard at\nany task you set me to.\nSure, mining's rough, but\nas long as the zeny's coming\nin, I'm happy. Heh heh heh~","...\n......","...\n......\n.........","Hey. Why are you\nlooking at me like\nthat? There's no idle\nchatting allowed at work.\nIf Canphotii catches\nyou, you'll be punished...","Oh wait...\nYou don't work here.\nI apologize, that kind\nof reaction's an old\nhabit for me, adventurer.","Do you know why a woman\nlike me has to work in this\nfactory? I'll tell you why...","My lazy husband, Gesin,\nis just lying there on the\nground! So I have to work\nin order to support us!","We can't rest for even\na second if we want to save\nenough money to become\nwealthy and powerful some\nday. Don't you understand?","Well, my husband obviously\ndoesn't! How can he not know\nhow the real world works?!\nHey, kick his ass for me if\nhe doesn't wake up soon!","There was a time\nwhen I dreamed of\nbeing an adventurer,\njust like you. But that\nwas a long time ago...","Now, I'm nothing but\na factory manager. Still,\neven if my job's not that\ngreat, I'm pretty satisfied.\nI'm sure people enjoy the\nproducts I oversee and all...","Maybe my life was meant\nto be this way, even if it's\nnot how I planned it. But the\ntime will come when I up and\nleave and travel the world\nonce I get my chance!","I hope the day will\ncome when I can meet\nyou out in that big wide\nworld and greet you as\na fellow adventurer.","Arrrgh!\nThis is killing me!\nWhy should I be rich?\nWhat's wrong with living\nwithin our means?","I've got no problem\nwith my current way\nof life, but the old ball\nand chain disagrees.\nWhy is she so obsessed\nwith riches and power?","Well, in any case, I'd\nlike to help her, but I can't\nget up! I'm exhausted and\nmy body is just overtaxed.\nI have no strength at all.","This is horrible~\nI should be resting\ninstead of worrying\nabout making money...","Good god!\nI'm so stressed!\nIt's been nonstop\nsince I moved here!","The work is tough and\nalready the boss hates\nme! I didn't move here\nfor this! Still, the pay is\ndecent so I guess I should\nendure just a little longer.","Here goes...!\nYo-heave-ho!\nYo-heave-ho~!","It's great that the\nfactory is making good\nbusiness and drawing\nin a lot of profit, but I still\nhave one major concern.","The amount of pollution\nthat this place is causing\nis horrific! We've got these\nmachines blowing out toxic\ngas all day long! The air\ncan't be safe for very long...","I mean, the air we're\nbreathing right now is\npretty foul and things\nare only going to get\nworse. How can we\nsolve this problem?","Staring at this\nbubbling hot liquid\nmetal gives me a good\nfeeling inside. It's like\nthat stuff can melt anything!","Imagine covering an\nentire street of people\nwith that stuff! Bwahah--\nOh, I'm sorry if I'm talking\ncrazy talk! I'm just kidding~","Machines are sooo\nconvenient. Just look\nat this contraption easily\ndo tasks that'd be tough\nfor me to finish alone.","Now this is what\nI call technology!\nSure, it takes effort and\nmoney to make one of\nthese, but what do I care?","I've got no problems,\nso long as this freaking\nthing keeps working the\nway I want it to!","I'm in charge of this\nblast furnace which\ncontains all of this\nboiling magma.","Even though it doesn't\nrequire actual labor, this\njob is pretty tiring. I've got\nto pay careful attention all\nthe time. It's pretty stressful.","Still, I'm proud of my job\nsince I have the responsibility\nof ensuring employee safety.\nAnyway, don't get too close\nto the furnace. It won't do if\nyou get burned on accident!","Hustle, hustle!\nPick up the pace!\nAnyone working too\nslowly will be punished!","Can't you understand\nthat?! Now go to your\nstation and get back to\nwork! Wait, are you even\nan employee? If not, then\nstop wandering around!","You're not supposed\nto be able to get in here!\nI can't believe they let you\nin! This requires extreme\ndisciplinary action!","\n Train Station\n","\n Hotel\n","\n Airship Airport\n","\n Laboratory\n","\n Airship Repair Shop\n","\n Weapon Shop\n","\n Factory\n","West - Laboratory, Airship Repair Shop\nSouth - Einbroch Front Gate\nNorth - Airport\nNortheast - Train Station, Hotel, Weapon Shop","Southwest - Airship Repair Shop, Laboratory\nNorthwest - Airport\nNorth - Weapon Shop, Hotel, Train Station","East - Train Station\nSoutheast - Hotel\nSouth - Weapon Shop,Factory\nSouthwest - Airport, Airship Repair Shop, Laboratory","East - Weapon Shop, Hotel\nSouth - Factory\nSouthwest - Airship Repair Shop, Laboratory\nNorthwest - Airport","Northeast - Train Station\nEast - Weapon Shop,Hotel\nSouth - Airship Repair Shop, Laboratory","This factory has a lot\nof things that need fixing,\npronto! I'm amazed that\nthe place is still operating!","Lucky for us, I hear that\nsome altruistic adventurers\nhave been donating materials\nto help keep this factory from\nfalling apart... Or worse.\nBut that's just a rumor.","*Sigh*\nEven if it is true,\nthere's nothing no one\nhere can do. Nobody has\nthe courage to challenge\nthe system, you know?","I...\nI better get\nback to work\nbefore I get\nin trouble...","Welcome to Geffen,\nthe City of Magic!","I don't know much about magic, but do you know what tastes\nmagical? Honey!","It's soooo sweet and delicious. I'm not sure if it's an\naphrodisiac, but I know for a fact that it will relieve you\nof fatigue and help you recover from wounds!","Hornets living in the grasslands spend their lives gathering\nnectar at the Queen Bee's command. Honey is made from the\nnectar they gather.","But that's not all. There's a special kind of honey that's\nmade for only Queen Bees to eat:\nRoyal Jelly!","Nothing can compare to the luscious flavor of Royal Jelly.\nAnd I think it's even better for you than ordinary Honey!","...Interesting.\nMost intriguing.\nOh! Let me tell you\nthis marvelous story~","While I was researching magic, I discovered this mysterious\nscroll. It describes this tree named Yggdrasil.","The leaves, seeds and fruit of Yggdrasil link every living\nthing in this world. According to this scroll, Yggdrasil is\nalso involved in the creation of the world.","Speaking of which, I've also heard of a rumor about a\nmiraculous tree in some land near Comodo. They must be\nconnected, I'm sure of it!","Hello!\nIsn't it a\nwonderful\nday today?","Well, I wouldn't know. I've been studying too hard to become\na Mage. I've been staying up all night, agonizing over\nanything that's magical.","*Sigh...*\nI especially worry about all the drawbacks to using magic.","Oh darn! It was really annoying when a long-ranged enemy\nfound me the last time I went exploring. That crummy monster\ndisrupted the casting of all my spells! I didn't hit it at\nall!","After that, I realized I needed some sort of weapon to\ncounter long-ranged attacks from enemies. Something that can\nattack from a distance...","Some sort of...\nSharp, piercing\nprojectile launcher, preferably made out of wood.","But where could\nI find something\nlike that?!","There was a skillful weaponsmith\nin Al De Baran who had 4 sons.\nUnfortunately he lost all of his sons\nwhile developing a powerful weapon.\nThe father survived alone from the tragedy.","How sad it will be for the father...\nBecause of the incident, the weaponsmith\nretired from his work and hid himself somewhere.\nAfter that, no one could ever see\nthe powerful weapon that he and his sons were developing.","I don't think that 4 sons of him\nwent to the heaven with the anxiety.","Please head north to enter Kunlun.\nI hope you will have a great time\nwhile staying in Kunlun.","I simply adore festivals.\nThat's why I love this town.\nThis town makes me feel like I am\nin the middle of a festival all year round.","We are proud to be an independent\nnation, and have been fighting\nagainst the evil invaders who've\nwanted to conquer this blessed land for many years...","But we have victoriously fended\noff every invasion! As long\nas we believe in ourselves,\nwe shall never forget the\nTrumphal Song that has helped us in our struggles.","The chief of this town is a man\nwho opens his heart to others.\nHowever, I have heard that there\nare some people who don't like his personality...","Well, I like my town. The Chief's\nefforts have made our town safer.\nI just hope other people feel the\nsame way about what he has done.","The men in our town, Kunlun, are\nall brave and courageous.\nBut, they are unable to get\nmarried. It's quite a shame really...","It's all because there are\nmore men than women.\nI am not even sure whether\nor not my son will be able to\nfind me a daughter in law.","Welcome.\nThis is the residence of Shi Yan Wen, the chief of Kunlun.","You better behave yourself while\nyou are here. If we see anything\nsuspicious, we'll arrest you in a heartbeat.","However, rest assured, you seem\nlike a trustworthy person.\nI'm sure nothing will happen. Enjoy your visit.","Welcome.\nThis is the residence of Shi Yan Wen, the chief of Kunlun.","You better behave yourself while\nyou are here. If we see anything\nsuspicious, we'll arrest you in a heartbeat.","However, rest assured, you seem\nlike a trustworthy person.\nI'm sure nothing will happen. Enjoy your visit.","Geez, just as I thought.\nThey won't sell alcohol to me.\nMaybe its cuz I'm too young...\nHmmm...I wonder how it tastes...","However, I know they're making\nsome tasty tea that even kids\nlike me can enjoy.\nIt makes my mouth water just\nthinking about this new tea.","Welcome to Kunlun!\nDid you enjoy all the incredible\nscenery on your way here?\nThe buildings may be small, but we\nall worked hard to build this city.","I have some miniatures of\nthe Rune-Midgarts Kingdom.\nYou can view all of Prontera in a\nsingle glance. The craftsmanship\non these masterpieces is quite stunning!","If you look around carefully,\nYou'll find all sorts of beautiful\nsights throughout the town.","Huh. So that giant\nair pouch can make\npeople float in midair?\nWould filling my tummy\nwith air work the same way?","I feel so blessed to\nlive in this quant, little\ntown. It's so beautiful, and\neveryone here is so nice~","For some reason, my older\nsister wants to move out of\nHugel as soon as she can. She\nSays that she's getting creeped\nout by the people that live here.\nDon't you think that sounds weird?","Ooh, I really want to\nhave that red bottle.\nI should ask my mom\nto buy me one. It doesn't\nlook too expensive, does it?","Hugel is a pretty\nsmall, homely village.\nEveryone knows everyone,\neverybody knows what\neverybody else is doing.\nIt's so suffocating!","There's no privacy in\nsmall towns. Someday,\nI wanna go out and\nlive in the big city~","You must not be from\naround here. Ah, you're\nan adventurer, right? Do\nyou know how I could tell?","It's because everyone\nwho's lived here starts\nto look alike after a while.\nAnd you certainly don't look\nas old as us. Well, have\na nice day, adventurer~","Yes, I'm an old man, but\nI can lick a whippersnapper\nlike you any day of the week!\nYou know, Hugel's got a longer\nlife expectancy than all the other towns. You wanna know\nwhy?","It's because the old\ncoots in this town refuse\nto just lay down and die!\nNow, c'mon! Lemme show\nyou how strong I am! Let's\nwrestle or something, kid~","You know, the people don't\nfight harmful monsters, they\njust protect themselves by\nequipping armor. That's\njust the way they are.","If you want to buy\nsome nicer armors,\nthen I suggest buying\nsome in a bigger city.","Welcome to the\nShrine Expedition Office.\nI'm Luda, a part-time\nassistant. My job is to\nkeep this office neat and\nclean, but look at this place!","Still, I think I can\nhandle this difficult task~\nThis room is the office for\nthe Schwaltzvalt Republic team,\nand the other is for the Rune-\nMidgarts Kingdom team.","I have to clean both rooms,\nso they keep me pretty busy.\nWhy don't you volunteer for\ntheir expedition? I know they\ncan't really pay you, but it's\na great chance to explore~","This part-timer is\ncompletely engrossed\nin his task of organizing\nfiles and books.","You know what's\nthe most beautiful\nplace in Jawaii?","It's 'Heart Island,' which is just a little north of here.\nThe water surrounding Heart Island is not that deep, so you\ncan just walk across if you're careful.","That's the best place to share an intimate moment with the\nperson\nyou love. It's perfectly secluded and such a beautiful area.","Of course, it's probably not\na good idea to go there by\nyourself if you're single.\nYou'd look like such\na pathetic loser!","Welcome to Jawaii!","Here, you can enjoy your\nhoneymoon without worrying about any interruptions. You\ndon't even have to bother with that notorious Single Army!","Well, there are a few monsters around, but you'll be okay as\nlong as you don't attack them first. Think of them as the\noriginal residents of this island, another sight to enjoy.","Ah, you must be a tourist.\nIf you're lost, just head West. Accomodations for newlyweds\nare located in the western part of Jawaii. The lodging here\nis\npretty amazing.","There are four different themed rooms, so you can choose one\nto your liking. There's a Guide around if you want to ask\nfor more information.","When you want to go back, please head to the NorthWest to\nboard\na ship to Alberta. If you want to sail to Izlude, there's a\nship waiting in the SouthEast.","Jawaii~\nJawa~ii~\nWhere you can\nfind happiness~","Oh, isn't it beautiful? You don't have to do anything other\nthan relax and breathe in the peaceful atmosphere. That's\none of the\nbest things about Jawaii.","Ooh! Sometimes we hold\nconcerts on this stage. If you're good at singing, why don't\nyou\ngo up on stage and sing\na song for us?","Jawaii~\nJawa~ii~\nWhere you can\nfind happiness~","I think we're really\nfortunate to be able to\nlive in such a beautiful\nand peaceful city like this.","It's just so nice to\nhave this pleasant weather,\nthese lush gardens and to\nmeet all of these kind people.\nLighthalzen is like Asgard\nin Midgard, heaven on earth~","*Sigh...*\nIt gets harder for me\nto move around as I get\nolder. That's understandable\nfor an elderly person, right?","Just the other day, these\nhoodlums in black suits\nwere yelling at me to get out\nof their way. But of course,\nI didn't move quickly enough.\nSo what did they do to me?","They punched me.\nRight in the womb!\nI know that I'm not\npregnant, but that's\nbesides the point. Never hit\na lady, especially an old one!","I think ''Lighthalzen'' is\nsupposed to mean ''crest of\nlight,'' though I hear that this\ncity was actually named after\nsomebody. Who knows for sure?","Still, it's a fitting\nname for the wealthiest\nand most luxurious city in\nall the Schwaltzvalt Republic.\nSo how do you like this place?","When I grow up, I want\nto become such a great\nperson that they'll make\na statue of me, just like\nthose statues over there.","Then people would be like,\n''Hey yo. That statue. That\nguy must have been great!''\nJust thinking about that\nmakes me feel so good!","That's it. I'm gonna\ngrow up as soon as I can.\nOoh, and I better grow tall\nand handsome so my statue\nwill be even more awesome.\nYeah. Yeah, good idea, Sung...","There are too many\nloving couples in this city.\nCuddling and kissing and\nhugging and necking. It's...\nIt's utterly distasteful.","I can't believe the\nindecency I see everyday\nnear my own home. Don't\nthey know better than to be\nso affectionate in places\nwhere the public can see them?!","Fortunately for the\nworld, I'm a bulwark\nof morality. In fact, I have\nno need for a woman. All\nI need are my ship models,\nteen novels and dominos.","I'm a completely well\nadjusted individual, which\nis why the authorities should\nlisten to me when I tell them\nto arrest couples for indecency!\nHand holding. Have they no shame?!","Oh no, I think I got\nlost again. The roads\nhere are so confusing!\nI've lived here for such\na long time and I still\ncan't find my way around...","Oh darling, the\nweather is so nice\nand pleasant today.\nI'm really glad we\ndecided to go take\na walk together~","...","...\n......","Ah...\nI just had the nicest\nnap. This nice weather\nnever fails to relax me.\nThe air here is so clean,\nnot like that Einbroch~","This clean, pristine\nenvironment is all thanks\nto the Rekenber Corporation.\nIt's incredible what they can\ndo with technology now, isn't\nit? Ahhh, it's so peaceful~","You know what I noticed?\nThe guards at the border\nto the slum seem distracted\nsometimes. I made use of one\nof their less attentive moments\nand basically jumped the fence!","But once I was in the\nslums, I was pretty bored.\nThere really isn't much to\ndo there. Which makes me\nwonder... Why guard it?","I can sense your\nlonging look within\nthe depths of my heart,\nbeating faster and faster\nwith a feverish passion~","Those eyes of yours...\nSo pure and so deep,\nlike glimmering pools\nof light. So, so beautiful...","I really wish that my\nson will be able to join\nthe Rekenber Corporation.\nThey certainly provide the\nbest jobs in Lighthalzen.","Although they're a large,\nmajor corporation, it's\nalmost impossible to get\nemployed by them. How\ndo people get hired there\nin the first place anyway?","I just step out to get\na haircut and now I'm\nlost. Boy oh boy, I hope\nI don't keep my family\nwaiting. *Sigh...*","Have you ever seen the\npeople who work in that big\ncorporation over there? I think\ntheir employees are all a bit\noff kilter for some reason.","I haven't been there\nmyself, but something\nstrange is happening with\nall the people who work there.","The youth in this city\nhave no appreciation for\ntheir elders. I've worked\nso hard to help build this\ncity for so many years and\nthis is the thanks I get?","Bah! If it weren't for\nus, Lighthalzen wouldn't\nbe as properous as it is\ntoday! Those kids don't\nknow that they owe their\nlives of luxury to us...","Good looks. Intelligence.\nExcellent manners. A strong,\nmanly chin and overpowering,\npiercing eyes. Perfectly balanced passion and charimsma. All\nthe\ngood things that ladies want.","But enough about me. Let's\ndiscuss how sorry I should\nfeel for any other man living\nin Lighthalzen. They don't hold\na candle to my studliness~","I've heard that there's a\nstrange kingdom out there\nthat's basically ruled by\nmagic and swords, where\nadventurers are enlisted\nfor the greater good.","So are you from\nRune-Midgard?\nWhat do you think\nof our city with its\nadvanced technology\nand economy? Huh...","Someday, I'd like\nto go visit the land\nwhere you came from.\nIt sounds so fantastic\nand romantic in a way...","The land around here\nis some pretty expensive\nproperty. Yes, it's perfect\nfor building my awesome palace!\nI don't have enough funds at the\nmoment, but the day will come~","Sure, I sell a lot\nof flowers here, but\nthe lease that this city\nmakes me pay cuts into\nmy profits. It's almost not\nworth renting this property.","I pay such a ridiculous\namount for the lease and the\nlaws here won't let me raise\nthe price of my flowers. Why\nare the city officals so greedy?","......\nThat lady, working\nfor that one company,\nKafra, Mafra or whatever.\nShe certainly is very charming.","Now, if I were\nthirty years younger...\nWait! I'm a rich and powerful\nman. I could ask her out now.\nHm? What's that look for?","Sure, manliness is quite\nattractive, but I think women\nappreciate a guy who could\nsympathize and talk with them\na little more. Don't you agree?","I might not be like Sefith,\nbut I guess I've got a cute\nsmile, a good personality and\nI'm a dandy to boot. Hopefully,\nmy honesty and loyalty will\nhelp me find someone good.","If you are experiencing\nany sort of inconvenience,\nplease do not hesitate and\nlet us know right away.","Please use the stairs\nat the northern end to\ngo downstairs so that you\ncan go to the Front Desk.\nThank you and I hope that\nyou enjoy your stay here.","OoooOoh~\nSoooo comfortable.\nDon't want to wake up.\nDon't want to get up.\nEver again. OoOoooh...","This hotel is nice\nand comfortable, but\nto be quite frank, the\ndrinks here are horrible.\nThey're unfit for drinking\nmen such as myself.","If this is the best hotel,\nI expect them to provide me\nwith the best alcohol. When\nI stay at a hotel, that's what\nI want. To spend the entire\nday not being sober.","It looks like that\ntoday I'll be heading\nout to the bar again...\nI just wish there were\nsomeplace quieter to drink.","This is the Couple Suite.\nA single can also check\nin here, but our hotel will\nprioritize couples when\nassigning this room.","This chair looks\nvery nice, but it really\nchills my bottom. Brr...!\nIt's a might uncomfortable!","You know what the\nperfect chair would\nbe like? It would be\nplush and have electronic\nmassage and heating controls...","Aaahhh Oooooh~\nIt's sooooo comfy~\nThe air's so fresh and\nthis couch is so plush...\nWhy can't home be like this?","I've been in those other\nhotels and let me tell you,\nthis place is the best ever.\nAfter a night's sleep over\nhere, I feel like a new man!","Oh sweet jiminy...\nThat Kafra Lady is so hot.\nWhat a body. And those glasses.\nI just gotta ask her out somehow.","Hm, but what should\nI do? A love letter? Naw,\nthat's kind of outdated.\nArgh, I can't think! Just\nlooking at her makes me feel\nso happy! Praise be to Kafra!","''Hospitality with a smile\nand total devotion to your\ncomfort.'' That's our motto\nin the Royal Dragon Hotel.\nPlease inquire at the front\ndesk if you wish to check in.","Welcome to the\nRoyal Dragon Hotel Bar.\nHow about a nice night\ncap before going to bed?","If you're looking\nfor a friend, you\ncan almost always\nmake one in this bar.\nAlcohol certainly is the\ngrease for social gears.","Oh yeah. I love-love-love\nbars. If I don't come here\nfor the booze, then I'm here\nfor all these beautiful ladies.","Weird. It's the very first\ntime I've tried this place's\nrum, but doesn't it taste like\npure sexiness to you? Huh...\nOh well, back to schmoozin'\nwith all the hot chicks~","Hey, you're from\nRune-Midgarts, right?\nPlease make yourself\nat home while you're here\nin Lighthalzen and have\nyourself a good time.","I hate it when guys\njust sidle up and sort\nof just skip Steps One\nand Two. And before you\nget all weird, Step Three\nis ''Ask for my phone number.''","I would just really\nappreciate it if one\nnice boy would just\ntalk to me for real.","I don't believe it...\nThis unlucky streak\nwill never end, will it?\nI lost all my Apples\nplaying Dice today.\nAgain. Oh man...","Okay. Okay.\nIf I just keep\nplaying, eventually\nI'll win. I mean, that's\nthe way the odds work, right?\nEven when they're against me...","I'm not big on drinking,\nbut the atmosphere in this\nplace is really nice. The\nmusic they play is always\nsmooth and relaxing...","Yeah, this is a real cozy\njoint. I recommend it to\nall you tourists, acutally.\nNow why don't you kick\nback and chill with me?","Am I just getting\nparanoid? I really\nthink that some of\nthe people I know\nare disappearing\nfor no good reason!","I mean, all of my close\nfriends are all alright,\nbut I'm starting not to see\ncertain acquaintances and\nfamiliar faces. Maybe I'm\njust thinking too much...","*Sigh...*\nOh, you poor\ndarling girl...","Man, if you were\ngonna take this whole\ncity and then sell it, what\ndo you think Lighthalzen's\nprice tag would be, eh?","I mean, this city\nis basically just made\nof money. Money is what\nmakes this city such a nice\nand pleasant place to live.","Greetings, adventurer.\nI'm Angela, a social\nworker for the Poor\nRelief Organization.","I've noticed that the\npeople living here have\nextremely bad health and\nit's not just because of\ntheir circumstances.","I've filed a report\nto my superiors, but\nthey haven't sent me\na response yet for some\nreason. I'm starting to get\na little worried about this...","Must work...\nMust focus...\nResist sleepiness...\nWhy do I keep coming\nhere? Ugh, h-horrible.","Hey youngster. You wanted\nadventuring advice? Okay.\nUm. Hm. Always. Brush.\nYour teeth. Brush them\neveryday. Oh, and don't\nforget to floss, either.","Now it's time for me\nto head back to work.\nI'll see you later, kid.\nSorry my advice was so\nlame-- I couldn't think of\nanything else to tell you.","So, the novel I ordered from\nthe Rune-Midgarts Kingdom\njust recently arrived. It's real good, by the guy who wrote\n''Roda Frog Adventure''\nyears ago. Remember?","Anyway, this new book,\n''Where the Red Plant Grows''\nis up for the Yggdrasilberry\nAward. I... I don't know why\nI was compelled to share that\nwith you. Seriously, I don't...","So... Very broke.\nWhy did I spend so much\nmoney on wine, women and\nsong? I regret it all, all the\npleasure I've had this month.\nYes, it was too much pleasure.","That's what happens\nwhen you're irresponsible\nwith your money. You really\nshould read this ''Anybody\nCan Be Rich'' book.","At long last, I've finally\nbought my own home. You\nshould invest your money for\nyour future too! Read this,\n''Anybody Can Be Rich!''\nIt's such a great book!","Hm? Sure, my last name\nis Rekenber and that's the\nsame name as our chairman,\nbut that's just a coincidence.\nI'm merely a normal employee.\nYeah, no special treatment...","This man here\nis motionless,\nand for all intents\nand purposes, is\nsoundly asleep.","What am I doing here?\nWaiting for my dream\nwoman to fall into my lap,\nwhat else does it look like?","Tall, blond, creamy\ncomplexion and smooth\nskin. That's right. Come\nright to Joshua, babes.\nI got my pheremone spray\non and I'm ready to cruise~","You know the men in\nblack suits? Boy, did\nI get a scare! They actually\ntracked me down to ask me\nall these weird questions!","They kept wanting to\nknow if I had ever met\nanyone from the Rekenber\nCorporation, if I've ever been\nUptown, that sort of thing. They\nreally scared the crap out of me.","Man, living in the\nslums is such a drag.\nNot only is life rough,\nbut all sorts of people\nthink they can push you\naround. I hate Lighthalzen...","Whiskey!\nI need me some\nhard liquor now!","Wha--? I didn't\norder this stinkin'\nrum! I want a man's\ndrink! Gimme whiskey!","Hey! Hey you...!\nD'you wanna, you\nwanna hear me tell\nyou a joke?! It goes...\nUm, it goes like this...","Hey riddle middle,\nthe cat and th--\nNo! No, damn it!\nThat's a song!\nNo, wait, that's\nnot a song either...","*Hiccup* I loooove\nthis rum! I caught a cold\nonce and one glass made\nit go away! 'Course, I slept\nfor a week too, but that don't\nmatter! Pshaw! Science...","Oh, the flavor is just\nso clean, but it's also\ngot a bit of a kick. I don't\nknow how to describe it.\nIts the taste of happiness?\nI'm too drunk to even tell!","This place is nice\nand usually pretty quiet.\nI like to come here after\nwork, have a drink and just\nchat with the bartender.","The rum here is incredibly\ngood too. It might even be\nthe best in the world. I dunno\nwhy, but for some reason, its\ntaste reminds me of teamwork~","Oh, I'm only here\nworking as a waitress\nto help out my father.\nThis job is so tiring, but\nit's nice to see people so\nrelaxed and having a good time.","When I get some time\noff, I'm going to explore\nLighthalzen and see all that\nthere is to see. But for now,\nit doesn't look like we've got\nany real shortage of drunks...","*Sob* I just got\ndumped! Yeah, I thought\nwe were gonna get married,\nbut obviously I was wrong!\nDamn it Sheryline! I loved you!","I usually don't care for\ndrinking, especially stuff\nlike gin or rum, but today,\nthis stuff tastes just like\nmy misery. This is all the\ncomfort I need, you hear?!","After ten years\nof marriage. My\nwife divorced me...","So I guess there's no\nplace for me but here for\nnow. I don't know what it is,\nbut the rum is really good\ntoday. Like, it's the flavor\nof relaxing, joyous relief~","You know, everyone\nis different, but I think\nhumans are similar enough\nthat we can all meaningfully\nconnect on some level, right?","Sure, a rich person might\nhave different problems than\na poor person, but the point\nis, they've both got problems!\nPain, pleasure, sadness, joy.\nThose link us all together.","So try not to be picky\nabout who's your pal and\nwho's not. We all need\nsomebody to be with, right?","One of the things I look\nforward to during my day\nis the drink I enjoy right\nafter work. It's the most\nrelaxing thing in the world.","Of course, there's\nmore to life than just\nhanging out in pubs and\nbars. The thing is, in my\ncase, pubs and bars are\nall I happen to need~","Do you know who I am?!\nJust look at this peg leg.\nI was in the Comodo War,\nSki Troop division! I lost my\nleg to earn your freedom!","H-hey! What's that\nlook for? What, you\ndon't believe me?!","This is a\nrestricted area.\nPlease keep clear\nif you do not have\nspecial authorization.\nThank you for your cooperating.","Oh phooey.\nThe same customers\nare always coming in,\nday after day. Can it\nget any less exciting?","Oh...!\nW-welcome~\nC-can I help you\nwith anything?","Greetings. This path\nleads to the Library and\nthe Laboratory. Please be\naware that these places\nare restricted from access\nby the general public.","Oh no...\nWhere did I put it?","The chairs here are\nso not ergonomic. And\nthey're uncomfortable too!\nBut it's sooo cool inside this\nbank and I just wanted to get\nget away from all this heat...","You know, maybe when\nI grow up, I'll be a bank\nclerk. That sounds like a\nreally nice job, don't you\nthink? It's laid back and posh...","I do so enjoy the\narchitectural structure\nof this bank. It's quite\nartistic with both classical\nand modern elements. Would\nyou not agree? Fascinating...","Oh, it's so comfortable\nin here~ Though, why are\nwe inside the bank when\nthe bank services aren't even\nworking? Yes, we're standing,\nbut we're doing it in comfort.","In fact, it's so\ncomfortable here,\nI think I'll refuse to leave.\nThough, I'm willing to change\nmy mind if you can find a place\nthat's even more comfortable.","Due to some critical system\nerrors, all of the bank services\nhave been temporarily stopped.\nWe apologize for any inconvenience and appreciate your\nunderstanding.","Oooh yeah...\nGoes down smooth.\nMorroc whiskey's the best!\n*Hiccup* Whoa, this stuff\nreally works fast! Heh heh~","Grrrrrr! Leave me alone!\nHow many times do I have\nto keep telling you? I've never\nhoarded item upgrade materials!\nI swear that I'm innocent!","Meh heh heh...\n*Hiccup* Believe\nit or notsh, I'm...\nwalkin on a... Air...\nNevah thought I could\nb-be sho freee-eeee-eee~","This guy\nis completely\nhammered out\nof his mind!","Let me go!\nLet me GO!!\nLET ME GO!!!\nI didn't do nuthin'\nwrong! I'm innocent!\n*Hic-Hic-Hiccup...*","What's wrong with\ndrinking and singing\nin the street, huh?\nIs it a crime to have\na beautiful tenor voice?!\nGet me outta this joint!","Tell me...!\nTELL ME...!!\nAdmit you did it!!","Damn it!\nI keep telling\nyou I'm not guilty!","*Sigh...*","You're wasting your\ntime. Just let me go.","So...\nHow's your mother?","That's none of\nyour business!\nShe's fine, I guess.","When was the last\ntime you've seen her?","I just told you,\nthat's none of\nyour business...!","You know, mothers\nthroughout the animal\nkingdom instinctively\ncare for their young.\nHumans are no exception.\nYours must be worried to death.","...\nMan...\nYou're starting\nto weird me out.","Funny thing about humans,\nthough. It seems to be their\nnature to lie, even when they\nknow they'll be caught. But\nlike all animals, they\ninstinctively fear pain...","N-no, no...\nYou gotta be...\nYou're bluffing.\nRight?","NO.\nYou're bluffing.\nTell me...!\nTELL ME...!!\nAdmit you did it!!","This Banquet Hall is used\nto hold events such as dinner\nparties with partners, clients\nand other associates, and press\nconferences. Of course, there's\nnothing going on right now.","Sometimes peace and quiet\nis a welcome change of pace,\nbut right now I'm feeling quite\nbored. I think I would rather\nbe busy than twiddling my\nthumbs, to tell the truth.","Shhhh! Hey, my brother's\n''it,'' so I gotta find a place\nto hide! Wait, would you just\nstand really still? I could\njust hide behind you! No?\nNuts! Olly olly oxen free!","Man... I hate being ''it!''\nI'm horrible at this game!\nAlright, okay, if I were my\nsister Luccet, where would\nI think I would not look for\nme? Of course...! The sewers!","I've heard that the\nRekenber Banquet Hall\nis also used to hold weddings.\nThat must be so wonderful~","Even if it is more expensive,\nI'd want to have my wedding\nhere. Marriage is only once\nin a lifetime, ideally, so I'd\nwant to make mine the most\nmemorable experience.","*Shhhhhhzzzz*\n*Shhhhhhzzzz*","Shhhhh....\nAaaaaaaahhh...","The employee turned his\nhead and peered into your\neyes through the black mask\non his face. Mereth stared\nwordlessly for a moment and\nthen began to dance a lively,\ncreepily jovial jig.","This is simply a pile\nof files, a smattering of\nbooks and a family portrait.","This desk is very\nneat and well organized\nin comparison to the other\ndesks you've seen in your\ntime. You take a moment to\nfully marvel at its tidiness.","Hee hee~!\nYou wanna hear\nsomething funny?\nI heard there's a bar in\nProntera where this guy\nsneaks singles into Jawa--","Noama...!\nThese machines are\nacting up again! Get\nover here right now!","What?!\nStop bugging me,\nI didn't do anything!","Crap. Crap! Crap\ncrap crap crap crap!\nThese desk machines aren't\nsupposed to work like this!","Noama...!\nThese machines are\nacting up again! Get\nover here right now!","What?!\nStop bugging me,\nI didn't do anything!","Jorje seems so cranky\nrecently. He's usually\nmore laid back than this.\nOh well, I hope that he\nfeels better.","Ooh, would you like\nto look at my miniature\ndoll collection? I love\ncollecting cute dolls!","You found a blackboard\nfilled with scribbling. You\ncan only read some of the\nmessages that have been\nquickly scrawled on it.","''Make sure everything\nis complete by XX 00.''\n- Jorje","Late Fee: 59, 990 zeny","''I want to have''\n- Ellette\n''I want $$$ too!''\n- Enoz\n''How about @@@?''\n- Ellette","''I wanna buy [#@$].''\n- Ninjose\n''Go buy it!''\n- Senyu\n''Working hard and buying hard\nis the best employee attitude.''\n- Mazwon","My mommy and daddy\nalways come home late.\nSo I eat dinner alone.\nAll by myself. Everyday.","Food doesn't taste as\ngood when you're not\neating with anybody.\nMaybe I'm just lonely.","This house is enormous...\nIt's clearly much too big\nfor a regularly sized family.\nAnd it takes me forever to\nmake sure that it stays clean!","It's not easy keeping\nthings neat and tidy when\nyou're responsible for acres\nof indoor living space. Being\na maid can be pretty hard...","I better dust extra\ngently around this vase.\nIt's worth ten million zeny\nand if it were to-- No. No!\nI'm not even going to think it!","Down there, the repairman\nis just finishing maintenance\non our chairman's private\nAirship. Can you imagine\nhaving one of those of your\nvery own to fly around in?","Yeah, the chairman of\nthe Rekenber Corporation...\nHe's a really powerful person.\nIt's almost scary what he can\ndo with his money, you know?","Sometimes the simple\npleasures can give you\nthe most happiness. For me,\ngoing outside and basking in\nthe sun is the greatest thing~","Yes, sunbathing in a quiet\nand relaxing place can be\nso refreshing. And if you're\ncareful about not getting a\nsunburn or a tan, a little sun\ncan be really good for you.","Curses...\nI've come to the\nwrong place to seek\nout a challenge. No\none here is really all\nthat mighty or competitive!","This whole city thinks\nit can buy power and safety\nwith money. They don't know\nthe value of a nice, friendly\nbrawl. Hopefully, I'll find a\nrival around here soon...","This city might have\nmore guards and rules\nthan other places, but\nI still don't know if it's\nreally safe to live here.","I mean, the reason we have\nthese rules is because of all\nthe unruly gangsters that can\nsometimes get into the city.\nI mean, it's relatively peaceful and all. But these rules...","It's good to be safe,\nbut I don't know if it's\na good idea to sacrifice\nour freedoms or standard\nof living, you know?","Oh, you youngsters.\nAlways traveling around\nand having adventures and\nfighting monsters. I certainly\nhad my fill of excitement back\nwhen I was your age, long ago.","Sure, I miss doing all\nof that, but now I'm content\nwith just relaxing and resting.\nStill, there are a lot of old folk who refuse to sit still\nlike this~","Granny may be happy\njust sitting around and\nenjoying the peaceful life,\nbut I'm not! I'm too young\nto just lay down and let\nthese days just pass by!","I wanna make something\nof myself. Maybe someday,\nI'll found a company as big\nas the Rekenber Corporation!","Unlike most places,\nLighthalzen has many\nbeautiful clothing and\naccessory shops. This\nplace is heaven to a\ntrendsetter like me~!","I don't know if you\nadventurers are interested\nin fashion, but you can trash\nyour old clothes and get some\nnew, unique and trendy gear\nover here in Lighthalzen~","Another hungry day...\nI don't have any money\nand even if I did, there's\nno place that sells food\nI'd actually eat. Oh, man.\nI'm barely living as it is.","I hear that the people\nwho live Uptown eat totally\ndelicious, gourmet food eight\ntimes a day! Hopefully it's just an exaggeration. 'Cuz if it\nwasn't, I'd be so mad...","A-ack...\n*Cough cough*\nWould you give me\nsome m-medicine?!\n*Cough cough haack*\nSweet Christmas, it hurts...","I sk-skipped work\nbecause I've been too\nsick t-to go. *Cough*\nBut now I don't have\nthe money to *Haack*\nbuy med-medicine...","Those rundown buildings\nin the slums are an eyesore\nthat offend the entire city!\nI just wish they would wreck\nthem down. What do I care\nabout the poor and needy?","I've heard that the\nRekenber Corporation\nactually created the\nenvironment in Lighthalzen\nthrough artificial means.","It seems like it'd take\na lot of investment, but\nartificially creating an\nenvironment isn't impossible\nwith the means available to\nthe Rekenber Corporation.","*Sigh...*\nStill, it's pretty\ndepressing to think\nthat the beauty of nature\ncan be manmade and\nequated to zeny, you know?","I don't like this.\nBut I don't like that\nidea either. What will\nI do for a new event, eh?","I need something\nmajor, something that'll\nreally shake up the world,\nsomething epochal, but what?\nHey, do you have any ideas?","Hmmm...\nThe employees seem\nto be having too much\nfun amongst themselves\nrecently. This does not\nbode well at all...","It looks like I'm\njust going to have to\nstart cracking that whip\nmore often and much\nharder. Ha ha ha ha!","Ack! I'm totally\nswamped with all this\nwork! But I don't wanna\ndo any of it. That's it!\nI totally need a break.","*Sigh...*\nI wonder if Saera\nwould ever consider\ngoing out with me?\nThat would be nice~","I am practicing my 'Claw of Dragon.' I not only need to use\nthe power of my fists, I must also condition myself\nspiritually.","Every martial art requires\nspiritual training since the\nmind controls the body.\nIf you've trained yourself spiritually, you can easily\nuse any part of the body!","If you are considering\nstudying the martial arts, you should first attain knowledge\nbefore jumping into the\nphysical training.","Learn about the martial arts\nand meditate on life's truths. First, you must find peace of\nmind before you can hope to master the mind and body.","Finally...\nI have mastered\nthe 'Claw of Dragon!'","Although there are eight basic steps, I had to learn the\nhistory of this art, and meditate, focusing on my spiritual\nimprovement,\nfor three years.","After that, my master finally started to give me the\nphysical training so I could use the eight steps of the Claw\nof Dragon. I've devoted myself to this art for thirty years.","I'm very proud that I've\nmastered this art ten years earlier than I expected. Now, I\nneed to study this form and improve it by correcting its\nweak points and enhancing its strengths.","I guess that would take me about ten years. But I'm not\ndisheartened by that at all.","When you're learning a martial art, you can't rush yourself\nand learn everything in a short period of time. It's\nimpossible! Plus, that isn't the essence of art...","Yeeeyap~!\nTaaaaaah~~!!\nHooo~.","Tah Tah Tah!\nTaaaaaah~~!!\nSchwooooooo~","Si!\nAyah!!","Dergh!\nDergh!\nSchwa--!","Yah Yah Yah!\nTaaaaaah~~!!\nWataaaaaaaah!","Yeeeyap~!\nTaaaaaah~~!!\nHooo~","Ho Ho Ho~\nMeeeerry Christmas !!","It's...\nIt's the original Santa Claus!","Ho Ho Ho~\nI'm Santa Claus, and I bring gifts to every good boy and\ngirl on Christmas!","If you want to leave Lutie, go outside town and head south\nto the first field that you see. You'll be able to find a\nmagical warp that will take you to Al de Baran.","Ho ho ho~\nMeeeeeeerry Christmas!","After that terrible incident wiped out the entire Morroc,\nRune-Midgard Kingdom has gathered us valunteers to help\nrestorations.","As important as it seems, everyone's being careful but there\nare always some that really don't realize the situation,\ndon't you think?","We're... We're flooded with work...","This work's like never-ending, no matter how hard we try!!!\nPeople of Rune-Midgard!! Please lend us a helping hand!!","Haw.... Whew... Ugh...","We're still unable to estimate the overall damage.","Adventurers' Union and Prontera Kingdom are putting their\nefforts on restorations as well as restraints of the\noriginal cause of the disaster.","Unless we settle the original cause, the damage will even\nspread out of Morroc. The only thing left is to get worse.","As bad as it seems, we can't even ask for more support.\nThis sure must be the worst thing ever happened in Rune-\nMidgard's history.","I wish I knew how bad the damage is, but we can't even\nestimate it. It's like shovelling sand against the tide..","The town's all shattered, but the real problem is the\ntowners.","It's a real pity to see those victims of the destroyed town,\nbut the witnesses of the disaster are so much shocked.\nThey're simply not normal now.","People are scared to death, but those are fortunate at\nleast.. cause.. many others got mentally ill and stuff..","The town's completely destroyed, but that giant triangular\nstructure hasn't been harmed at all. Maybe it's protected by\nsome kinda special power.","You know...Those giant, triangular buildings at the\nNorthWest corner of Morroc known are known to us as\nPyramids...","Those things have been around here for thousands and\nthousands of years. No one knows when and why they were\nbuilt, or who built them.","All we know is that tons of monsters live inside those weird\nbuildings. You might wanna stay away from those really\ndangerous places.","Those monsters in the Pyramid would be very, very sensitive\nto sweet flash smell of people....","I've devoted my life to researching the mysterious pyramids\nnear Morroc. I haven't been able to concretely confirm\nanything yet, but...","I'm sure that the largest pyramid contains the tomb of the\nancient king, Osiris! I'm willing to stake my life on it!","I remember I said the bandits of desert are the desert\nwolves.. Those bastards always roam around in a bunch and\nthey would get so cruel and outrageous if one of them got\nattacked.","They are so vicious, and I'm telling ya, I'm no kidding. You\ncan only find some bones and rotten milk in the backpack\nafter these wolves sweep through.\nThose things are so mean and vicious..","But the thing is that.. I even kinda feel those merciless\ncold-blooded monsters are nothing to be afraid of, compared\nto what has happened in Morroc. Morroc is already a hell.","I work in the trading business, so I always have to cross\nthe hot, dry Morroc Desert on business.","But I can't do that anymore.","Now that I can't, I kind of miss the old days.","Like this one time, while I was in the middle of the desert,\nI got so thirsty that I caught a cactus.. but before I was\nable to cut it, it slapped me! Then it shot me in the arse\nwith all these needles...","Later, I learned that it wasn't a normal cactus I found, but\nthe monster we call 'Muka.'\nNow I come to think of it, it was fun as much as dangerous.","The undisputed queen of jewels has to be the Diamond. After\nlooking at it just once, no one can deny its beauty.","Many factors determine its value, but the most important\nthing is its size.","It should also be a perfect crystal, not cracked or chipped,\nif you want to sell the Diamond for a lot of zeny.","But look! The hardest stone in the world got broken in two!","I know it's not the time to worry about some gemstones but..\nthis.. was my everything..","Wait a second..! Are you perhaps an adventurer? Welcome!\nHow's your trip?\nHeh heh~ Let me tell you a story. You know I just got out of\nthat Tavern, there, huh?","I heard the Satan Morroc has revived. It just got out of\ncracking the time and the space blar... hic~","Ah... I kinda wanna see that Satan with my own eyes, but! I\nreally shouldn't. I shouldn't even dream of seeing that\nSatan in person.","But I think there'd be nothing to lose if you, a person of\nbravery, who came through the wile desert try to find it,\ndon't you think? Teehee~ Don't forget to buy me a drink when\nyou find it!\nHic!","Anyway, do you know where we are? I just had a little drink\nat a tavern, but all of a sudden, the whole town's\ndisappeared when I got out.. or, some five hundred years\nhave passed???!","... That day... I saw the bloody moon in the sky. It was too\nsilent that it felt so spooky.","Not even a whistle of dry wind, and the air so heavy and\nstuffy, I could hardly breathe.","But then, Bang! It was right that time that I saw the\nenormous amount of smoke rising up at the Castle of Morroc\nwith an earsplitting sound.","All happened so fast. The Oasis of the Castle was all dried\nup and the town was destroyed. And... and that voice... I\nheard a voice.","Blood... Blood is what it takes to pay for the soul... and\nthat dark sound of laughter...\nAah!!! It's... It's still ringing in my ears!!! Aahhhhh!!!!","- It'd be better not to disturb him anymore -","-Crying-","I'm so scared! Where's mom and dad...! hhooooo... Where's\nour house...","Please stop crying, Eliese... You could even faint if you\ncry all day long, you know...","No! No... Mommy... Daddy....","............... Let's stop crying, Eliese...","Nooooooo... Mommy... Daddy....!!","Mom and Dad are now...","No...... noooooo...","Right, you love ice-cream, don't you? I.. I can get you an\nice-cream if you stop crying. Don't cry, Eliese, please..\nOk? Don't...","Our dear Csar Alexsay III is in the palace.\nHe rules over Moscovia.\nPlease be careful not to cause him any trouble.","I don't allow any living person\nto come in this place!","A long time ago,\nwhen Payon was still\ndeveloping, many of the\nvillagers lived in poverty.","Many families had to struggle to survive, and often could\nnot even afford to properly bury their dead. Some people\nthrew their dead into the cave near the village.","So in that cave, it is said that there are many walking\nZombies,\nthe dead who cannot rest in peace and are unable to pass on\nto the next world.","The Zombies, upon sensing the warmth of a human, begin to\nassault them, but that doesn't mean these Undead hold a\ngrudge against\nthe living.","Their rotten bodies can't leave the cold, dark and damp\ncave, so it's instinctual for them to attack warmth which\nwould speed up the decomposition of their bodies.","The Zombies in the Payon Cave\nmay be spooky, but their story\nis also kind of tragic.","From your attire,\nI can see that you\nare a stranger here.\nWelcome to Payon.","You must be a well-experienced fighter, otherwise you'd\nnever be able to arrive here after passing the steep,\nmountainous areas and dangerous creatures surrounding this\ncity.","I'm no expert at fighting, but someone once told me that\nsheer strength alone won't be able to win some battles.","Sometimes, you may encounter creatures protected by a hard-\nshell that don't be damaged by physical attacks. Only\npsychic power, like Magic, can easily defeat such creatures.","Of course, not everyone can study magic. The point is that\nyou should keep different kinds of friends and comrades\nclose to you, as you can't possibly handle every situation\nby yourself.","I remember the story my dearly departed grandfather has told\nme.","It's about this Amulet that possesses an Evil Power.\nWith it, you could awaken\nthe Dead from the Grave.","Well, I'm not sure if it's true or not. But, I wonder, what\nwould happen if I used it to summon\nmy grandfather from the other realm....","Never think\nof such a thing...\nMy son.","EEEEEEK-!\nWhat was that?!\nG-grandpa...?","...","...\n......\n...\nG-God...?","Welcome to Prontera.","Outside the safety of the city, there is a pink beast known\nas Poring.","Though it's cute in appearance and does not actively harm\npeople, Poring is known to absorb items that are on the\nground into its own body.","So if there's something on the ground that you want to pick\nup, be careful lest it be consumed by a Poring. Then\nagain... Porings are pretty weak...","The green colored Poporing is tougher than Poring. Newbies\ngenerally make the mistake of attacking it without being\naware of its power... So be careful!","Did you know?","The larva of Creamy is Fabre. So, those green little wormy\nthings are actually the babies of those pinkish, purply\nbutterfly things you see around.","But before Fabres can become Creamys, they go into a pupa\nstage. When that happens, they turn into these dark purple\ncocoons we call Pupa. Simple, huh?","There's another monster that goes through a really big\nchange... Pickys.","Pickys are so cute when they're young, but when they grow\nup, they turn into those big, gawky looking Peco Pecos. Talk\nabout awkward puberty.","The weather was nice on my day off so my family and I went\nfor a picnic. We chose to go to a slightly secluded area\nwhere I saw something really interesting...","It was a large group of Giant Hornets! What was even weirder\nwas that they were all controlled by this one Queen Bee,\nfollowing her every command.","They might just be bugs, but I think they've got the right\nidea. Men really ought to take commands from us women... We\ndo things right!","Although many monsters may look the same, be careful! There\nare variations among monsters that have the same basic form.","One monster, that looks just like a peaceful and weak one\nthat you've already encountered, may actually be wild and\nferocious!","You can tell these kinds of monsters apart by their body\ncolor. Wilder and more powerful monsters have more dangerous\nlooking colors.","Behold...\nMighty Odin!\nGod of wisdom!\nGod of war!","Here, in Rune-Midgard, we serve Odin, the fearsome god who\nsacrificed one of his eyes in order to acquire wisdom.","The statue you see behind of me is a sculpture of mighty\nOdin. But, it's a shame because it's such a bad likeness.","I mean, this statue is totally different from our image of\nOdin. I guess the sculptor took too many artistic liberties.","I bet the first time you saw this statue, you thought, 'Oh,\nwhat a nice muscle man on a horse.'","But this statue is obviously not muscular enough, not godly\nenough to fairly represent a god! Maybe if he had a halo?","Here in the Eastern branch of the Prontera Library, we\nprovide Monster Encyclopedias in which creatures are\norganized by their properties. We also have books on\nMerchant and Blacksmith skills.\nOoh~! The other branch of our library also has many\ninteresting things to read! So if you get a chance, you just\nmight want to visit.","The Prontera Culvert sewers have been left unattended for a\nlong time. Now that place is infested with Thief Bugs!","These Thief Bugs seem to quickly grab items dropped on the\nground, and then run away with them... They're even more\nannoying than cockroaches!!","I dunno if you'll believe me, but I saw the weirdest thing\ndown in the Culvert Sewers...","I've been training in the 3rd level for so long that there\nisn't anything that I don't know about in that area. But\nwhen I finally went to the 4th level...","There, I saw a shimmering light. I was completely captivated\nand went to approach it. It must have been some sort of\nbeautiful fairy...","But when I got\nclose enough,\nI saw it was\na Thief Bug!","I've never seen a Thief Bug shining with light before! Man,\njust when you think you've seen it all...","H-hey!\nWhat are\nyou doing here?!","Don't you know there's a Demon living in this forest?! I\ncan't guarantee your safety\nif you go in!","*Sigh...* The last guy that entered this place haven't come\nback at all. He didn't listen to me and went in to gather\nHerbs or something dumb like that...","Whaaaat a stupid guy. Why would anyone want to throw his\nlife away just to collect some silly Herbs?","Loomin, the boy\ntrapped in the Ice Cave.\nClass: 1st\n\n\n\nThe pope was born together\nwith a twin brother, a fair\nskinned boy with pale skin","and silver blonde hair. This\nhad never happened before\nand presented a unique problem\n\nHigh Priest Niren acted as\ntheir maternity nurse and\ncame to Rachel, where the\ntwins were cared for by the\nPriests. They all argued","over the boy's ultimate fate...\n\nNo one doubted that the boy\nwas spiritually powerful, but\nwas he a sacred complement to\nhis sister, or a great evil that\nwas in direct opposition to\nher? It was a grueling debate\n","In the end, the High Priests\ndecided that the boy posed\na great risk to their society\nPeople may not consider the\npope's birth as divine if they\nknew she had a twin brother.\n\nHowever, not wanting to fear\nthe wrath of the gods, the","High Priests did not kill the\nboy. Instead, they sealed\nhim in the Ice Cave.\n\nThe High Priests made\na contract with Ktullanux,\na fearsome ice monster, to\nguard the boy's prison, and\nto insure that no one would.","May Freya bless\nyou, and give you an\nabundance of health,\nwealth, joy, and happiness!","Freya is the goddess of\nlove and beauty. Do you\nthink that if I pray hard\nenough, she'll help me\nget a really pretty girlfriend?","I've never seen our pope\nbefore, I hear that she has\nsilver blonde hair and really\nwhite skin. Daddy says that\nonly one girl is like that\nin every generation.","My daddy says the pope is\nvery special to us because\nshe's Freya. I mean, Freya\nis a goddess, but she also\nbecomes people like us to talk\nto us. Well, just the priests...","I don't get it all,\nbut it sounds like\nshe's a secret princess.\nDoesn't that sound so nice?\nBut when I tell that to Daddy,\nhe gets so mad at me! Oh, well.","You are at Cheshrumnir,\nthe hallowed grounds occupied\nby our pope, Freya's mortal\nincarnation. In respect for\nher Excellency, I expect you\nto enter with a pious heart.","If you open this door, you\ncan go inside this house,\nand live in one of the rooms!\nThen, you can add your couches\nand a bed, and all of your stuff!","All you gotta do is...\nUgh! Turn this knob\nand... Grrrrah! Open\nthis door... But it's\nalmost impossible..","It's been so long\nalready! I can't find\nHimuhimu! Hide-and-Seek\nshouldn't take this long...","Oh, I'm already hungry...\nHimuhimu, come out so\nwe can go home and eat!\nHimuhimu! I give up!\nH-Himuhimu...?","Zzzz...Z...\nAnku, you'll never\nfind m... never find\nme here... Zzzzz...\n... So hungry...","Welcome to Rachel\nthe capital of Arunafeltz.\nPlease ask our guide\nat the center of the city\nfor information and\nguest services.","Bwahahaha! Somehow,\ndrinks taste much better\nduring work hours!","All of Arunafeltz believes\nin the goddess Freya, but\nthere are those of us that\nare more seriously involved\nin adoration and worship.","First, there are ''Freya's\nFollowers,'' men and women\nlike me that dress in holy masks\nand garments. I realize that our\ndress may seem a bit peculiar\nto you, but that is our way.","Then, there are the Priests\nwho dress in clean, white\nflowing robes. They work in\nthe temple and serve the\ncommunity as religious leaders.","Among these priests are\nthe elite High Priests that\ndirectly assist our pope.\nThey wear more colorful\nclothes as a sign of their\nhigher status in Rachel.","All of us work tirelessly\nto bring prosperity to\nArunafeltz, and to carry\nout the teachings of our\nbeloved goddess Freya.","Cheshrumnir...\nIt is said that one\nday, our goddess Freya\nwill descend to this place\nin all of her glory. I hope\nthat I live to see that.","......\n.........\n............","She is completely\nimmersed in deep,\nmeditative prayer.\nIt'd be rude to\ndisturb her now.","Look at these flowers.\nAren't they so beautiful?\nI've spent a lot of time\ncultivating this flower garden.","I think it's Freya's\nwill for us to\nbring as much beauty into\nthe world as we can. What\ndo you think about that?","Once again, I didn't get\nany sleep yesterday... I'm\npraying so hard for Freya's\nsecond coming. I'm exhausted,\nbut I feel pretty good about\nmaking that small sacrifice.","You have done well,\nmy brother. I am certain\nthat Freya would be proud\nof all your effots.","Shh! I'm playing\nHide-and-Seek. Would\nyou leave me alone, please?\nI don't wanna get caught again!\nMaybe it's because I always\nuse the same hiding place...","Oh my Freya! You scared me!\nI thought you were one of the\nkids playing Hide-and-Seek!\nAck! Get away, get away!\nCan't let them find me!","Where are yoooou~\nCome out, come out\nwherever you are~","What the Freya?\nWhat's a grown-up\ndoing around here?\nCan't you see I'm\nplaying Hide-and-Go-Seek?","- He is almost sleeping but he is still managing to hold a\ncup with a drink in it. He must be really tired-","Mr. Niels is at the table in the\ncorner. He has many interesting\nstories about the world.","I am not sure where he has been\nthis time. He just laughs and\nsays 'I don't think I am fit\nfor this teaching job.'","In the meantime, people keep\nvisiting Mr. Niels... and I\ncan't help but wonder...\nWhere has he gone?","Umbah umbah woogawoo...\noops, sorry! I'm so used\nto speaking in Utan by now.\nIt's a pleasure to meet you.","I never imagined that I would\nmeet another person from\nthe homeland in this village.\nHahahahah~!","I came here to seek strong people\nto help me master my fighting\nskills. But I was soon frustrated\nbecause it took me a long\ntime to learn the language...","Well, now I am kind of used to my\ncircumstances. Even though it\ntook me a while to used to\nUtan culture. Hahahaha~!","But you know what was the weirdest\nthing I found out about Utan\nculture? At first the Utan men\nseemed to have, shall we say, a\nstrong species preservation instinct.","There are many Utan playboys in\nthis village. Some may think\nthe Utans are primitive in\nthis respect, but...","As I learned more about them,\nI eventually realized that their\ncourtship rituals are actually\nmore advanced than anything the\nRune-Midgard culture has to offer.","It's really quite fascinating.\nI'm actually still learning\nquite much from the Utan\nplayboys and their awesome methods.","I love cacti. They're\nthe most beautiful plants\nin the desert. Sometimes,\nthey're the only signs of\nlife in a barren land.","If you feel a stirring\nin your heart when you\nlook at a cactus, you\nmust appreciate the\ndesert's true beauty.","Well, I don't know if\nI can find anyone that\nfinds the desert as\nwonderful and enchanting\nas I do. It's a pity, really.","Welcome to Veins, the\ntown near the Temple of\nCheshrumnir. You may think\nthis is a dreary desert town,\nbut you'll find that it's as\nlively as any other place.","Sure, there are a few\ncharacters in town, like\nthat cactus loving loony\nover there, but not everyone's\nlike him. There's lots of nice,\nkind people that you can meet.","Well then, I hope that\nyou enjoy your stay~","Geez, why is our weapon\nshop so boring? Nothing\nthere but the same ol'\nregular junk. Sad to say,\nthere's nothing special.","Wouldn't it be great\nif there was a shop that\nsold the legendary godly\nweapons? Of course, that's\nasking a bit too much.","Though we're in the\nmiddle of the desert,\nour enemies continue\nto threaten us. Fools!\nGoddess Freya will\nalways protect us!","So long as we continue to\ntrain, Freya will watch over\nus and bless us with victory\nover our foes. That, friend,\nis the power of faith.","Whoa, get out of here!\nCan't you see that I'm\nplaying hide and go seek?!\nMove before they find me!","Gosh, where could she\nbe hiding? I hate being\nit... There's so many places\nto hide around here. There\nmust be someplace I haven't\nchecked yet... Let's see...","Praise be to Freya\nfor blessing me with\nlong life, but I wonder\nif I've fully lived life.","I don't have any regrets\nor doubts, but maybe there\nare a few things I missed\nout on. I guess an old man\ncan't help but think about\nthese sorts of things...","Cacti are wonderful,\nthey're the most beautiful\nplants in the desert. Yes, we\nmust cherish and nurture them~","Regular cacti are\npretty uncommon, but\nI hear there's a kind of\ncactus that roams the desert\nand makes loud, obnoxious\nnoises. How can that be true?","What do you want?\nSorry, but I'm just\na normal guy with normal\nproblems. Nothing that\nI can't solve on my own.","Unless... You can do my\ntaxes? Pay off my mortgage?\nNo? Heh. Didn't think so.","What's an adventurer\ndoing here in such an\nisolated, dreary town?\nShouldn't you be looking\nfor adventures? Take it from\nme, this place if bo-ring.","Whoa, it's been a while\nseen I've seen tourists\nin town. You might think\nthere's nothing here, but\ntake a closer look. You\nmight learn something.","Just like people, you\ncan't know everything about\na place with only a glance.\nIf you give it a chance, I'm\nsure you'll find something\nto like about this town.\nand try to find things that mind interest you?","What do I mean by ''a\ncloser look?'' Heh, you'll\nsee... Maybe. Hahahaha!\nOh, forget it, it's not\nthat important anyway.\nMay Freya bless you~","I really want to look\ninside the temple, but\nit looks so scary from\nthe outside! I wonder\nwhy it's like that?","Don't get me wrong:\nI'd give my life in Freya's\nname, but that so-called\ntemple just looks so strange\nand suspicious. How can it\nbe a place of worship?","I guess you can tell\nfrom this withered tree\nthat our town is short\non water. I guess that's\na natural consequence of\nliving here in the desert...","When I look down on\nVeins from here, I've\ncome to realize many things.\nI don't think you'd understand\nno matter how much I explained.","I suppose it's one of those\nthings that you learn with age.\nYes, there's no substitute for\nexperience when it comes to\nsome things. You'll see.\nYes, like secret knowledge.","This isn't good.\nThe elderly outnumber\nthe youth here in Veins.\nWe're too close to becoming\nsomething of a retirement\ncommunity. You see it, right?","I guess the young people\naren't content living here\nsince we lack a lot of the\nmaterial excitement of other\ntowns. They can't appreciate\nwhat's really special here...","People cherish water\naround here, but I've\nsomething even more\nprecious to me. Yes, even\nmore precious than water...\nYou guessed it--true love.","We actually started dating\nhere, so this place really\nmeans a lot to me. It's my\nfavorite spot for spending\ntime with my girl. Hahaha~","Well, I'm actually\na little tired of coming\nhere all the time. I kind\nof want to try someplace\nelse, but I also know he\nreally loves coming here.","It would actually be\nkind of sad if we stopped\ncoming here altogether.\nI'm just happy so long\nas he's with me~ Hoho~","Why don't you take\na look at my goods?\nI've got many things\nthat might interest you~","Praise be to Freya,\nwho watches over us,\nand blesses us with\nfood and drink. Don't\nyou think that's great,\nyoung adventurer?","Owning a lot of stuff\nmight seem great, but\nmany things aren't that\nvaluable when you think\nof them in terms of\nreal emotional value.","Well, that might have been\na dangerous remark when\nI'm trying to sell things to\ncustomers. Still, I wish\nI could carry a wider\nselection of goods.","Of course, we're here\nin the middle of the desert,\nso maybe I'm asking too much.","Hey! Do you think\nI can reach the bridge\nover there if I jump\nfrom over here? Do\nyou think you can try it?","What?! You can't do it?\nWell, I'm gonna be different\nwhen I grow up! I'm gonna\nbe the world's best jumper!\nI'm gonna be able to jump\nall the way to the mooooon!","The clothes we make here\nare high, airy, and sewn\nwith high quality fabric.\nOf course, we need to wear\nstuff like this since the\nweather is unbearably hot.","The fabric? Well,\nI'll give you a hint.\nIt's made of something\nrelated to camels. Heh!\nI'll leave you to figure it\nout on your own. Haha!","Let me tell you a secret.\nBut promise not to tell\nanyone else about it, okay?","When the time comes,\nthe Temple of Cheshrumnir\nwill open up and the giant\nFreya robot will launch!\nIt'll destroy every country\nexcept Arunafeltz!","That robot can blow\nhurricanes from its mouth,\nand shoot lightning from\nits horns, and it can fire\nits fists away, and its\nchest is a flame thrower!","..............................\nYou don't believe me, either.\nWhat did you just say? Zinger?\nAmazing Z? The hell's that?","Argh! I'm a war god\nprotecting Goddess Freya\nand Arunafeltz! Ahhhhh!\nDeath to all our enemies!","Burn, heretics, buuurn!\nDestroy your homes, your\nfamilies, and build a new\nperfect world for Freya!","Hee hee! Doesn't that\nsound wonderful! When\nI grow up, I wanna be\nthat kind of hero!","Fr... Fr...","Fr...","Praise Freya! *Keck*\n*Cough cough* Fre...\n*Cough* Praise Freya!\nFreya! Conquer those\nthat blaspheme you! Let\nme see it before I die!","I have never regretted\n*Cough* my faith in you,\nmy goddess! *Keck* May\nthe suffering of all our\nenemies drive them to\nmadness before death!","I wonder what my\nstanding with Freya\nis like. Hopefully, she\nwill take mercy upon me\nwhen I leave this world.\nMy days here are numbered...","Huh? You don't live here.\nAre you... Are you a traveler?\nYou musta been to so many\nother places, huh? What\ndo they look like? I want to\ntravel too when I grow up~","I like this town, but I want\nto see how other people live.\nThe grown-ups think it's a bad\nidea, though. They say Freya\nhates it. Is it that bad that\nI can't stop wondering?","Oh. You must be\nsightseeing. Um,\nVeins is a small town,\nvisit Cheshrumnir Temple?","I hope you enjoy\nyour stay. Now if\nyou'll excuse me, I'd\nlike to continue with\nmy prayers to Freya.","Oh, gracious Freya, your\nservant humbly beseeches\nyou on bended knee...\nHeal me of this infirmity!\nThe body is droopingly limp,\nbut the spirit is willing...!\nmust be... Cheshrumnir Temple.","You know what's good\nabout the desert? No?","The desert makes you\nstronger. Understand\nwhat I mean? Heh, you'll\nknow as you spend more\ntime here in the desert.","Unbelievable!\nWhat kind of country\nis this?! How can you\nlock me up just because\nI don't believe in Freya?!","This isn't civilized!\nYou're a bunch of savages\nif you can't respect my\nbeliefs, you know that?\nSomeone, someone help!","This place ensures that\ndangerous criminals aren't\nthreatening the publi--\nWait. Why are you even\nhere?! This place isn't\nsafe for you! Leave!","I'm grateful that our\ntown is relatively peaceful.\nIf it were any other place,\nthat tiny cell would be\ncrammed full of criminals.","Thank Freya that I've\nbeen assigned to such\na peaceful, quiet place.","*Pant Pant*\nI must study as hard as I can\nfor the grace of Goddess Freya.","I really believe that\nI can serve Freya one of\nthese days if I can just\nexpand my knowledge.","It's too hot...","So sweaty...","...............\n...............\n...............","...............\n...............\n...............","Tricked you!\nThought I was dead,\ndidn't you? Hahaha~","The drinks in this\ntown are so... They're...\nThey're so damn strong!","Why...\nWhy does the ground\nkeep wobbling?! It's...\nIt's like it's trying to\nbetray me! Every time!","*Hiccup*","It's nice when a town\nis peaceful and quiet...\nBut it's lame when a\ntavern is dead like this.","Well, there's good\nand bad points to\neverything. Hopefully\nthings will pick up\naround here as more of\nyou adventurers come visit.","There's nothing but\nold people and children\nin this town. Where's a\ndecent man worth marrying?\nThere's a few bachelors that\nare my age, but... Well...","They're all too hairy or\ntoo muscular. I don't think\nI'll be able to get married\nanytime soon! Oh, the misery!","Well, our town doesn't\nhave a choice but to\ndefend itself in dangerous\ntimes. The young men we\nhave here are all buff and\ntough to protect us.","They may not be beautiful,\nbut they have kind and\ngentle hearts. It's a pity\nthat the women here\nare more concerned\nwith appearances.","Don't judge a book\nby its cover, but\nby its contents.","This storage solely\nexists for serious drinkers.\nIf it's ever shut down,\nI think everyone in town\nwill riot. Crazy, huh?","Veins is famous for its\nwide variety of delicious,\nirresistable liquor. Just one\nsip's enough to hook you.","Praise Freya for\nblessing us with the\ngift of awesome liquor.\nHer graciousness, her\ncompassion, her liquor\nis limitless. Let us pray.","I really want to\nask out the woman\nright in front of me.\nDo you think she'll...?","Crap! Did I say that\nout loud? I-I-I really\ndidn't want her to hear!","I heard all that...\nGosh, he's so clueless.\nI don't hate him, but he\nshould show a bit more\nbackbone if he wants\nto impress me. Hmmm...","If you enjoy a good,\nstiff drink, then you have\nto stop by Veins Tavern~","If you don't love\ndrinking, then Veins\nTavern is the perfect\nplace to learn! ...To\nlove... drinking...","Isn't the sun so hot?\nDoesn't it make you feel\nso thirsty? Well, you may\nwant to consider quenching\nthat nasty thirst with liquor!","My job is to serve\ndelicious, life giving\nliquor to my customers to\nrelieve their parched throats.\nSeeing their drunken smiles\nreally makes my day~","A lone wolf of the desert.\nThat's me. Well, that's why\nI'm drinking here alone.","Sweet Freya, these\ndrinks are so good.\nI could drink all day.","Man, the world is just...\nIt's just desires...!\nFaith? It helps, you\nknow? Cuz-cuz desires\nare all just nothing!\nThey're nooooooothing!","Argh! What is life?!\nI don't know what to\nbelieve anymore! Freya!\nFreya looooves you!","My name is Sergiof,\nthe fighter who\nserves Granny.","I will tell you about Grand Peco which is a high level Peco\nPeco. Grand Peco is faster than Peco Peco and is quite\naggressive.","It attacks using its strong bill and many Peco Pecos follow\nit. There's quite a difference in power between Peco Peco\nand the Grand Peco."};
#endif
